ViennaRNA Package — Disclaimer and Copyright
============================================

RNAfold.wasm in this directory is a standalone wasm32-wasi build of the
`RNAfold` program from the ViennaRNA Package, version 2.7.2
(https://www.tbi.univie.ac.at/RNA/, https://github.com/ViennaRNA/ViennaRNA).

Upstream license (verbatim, file COPYING of ViennaRNA-2.7.2):

  The programs, library and source code of the Vienna RNA Package are free
  software. They are distributed in the hope that they will be useful
  but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
  MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.

  Permission is granted for research, educational, and commercial use
  and modification so long as 1) the package and any derived works are not
  redistributed for any fee, other than media costs, 2) proper credit is
  given to the authors and the Institute for Theoretical Chemistry of the
  University of Vienna.

  If you want to include this software in a commercial product, please contact
  the authors.

  Note that the file ./src/ViennaRNA/plotting/naview.c has its own copyright
  attached.

Attribution
-----------
ViennaRNA Package, Institute for Theoretical Chemistry, University of Vienna.
Lorenz, R. et al. "ViennaRNA Package 2.0." Algorithms for Molecular Biology
6:26 (2011).

naview EXCLUDED
---------------
The separately-copyrighted file src/ViennaRNA/plotting/naview/naview.c is NOT
part of this build: the Naview radial-layout plotting algorithm is excluded
(configure flag `--disable-naview`), and no naview symbols are present in the
binary. Plotting/GUI/Perl/Python/SWIG components are not built.

Build provenance
----------------
  Source:    ViennaRNA-2.7.2 release tarball (pre-generated ./configure +
             gengetopt *_cmdl.c parsers; NOT a git checkout)
  Toolchain: wasi-sdk 33.0 (clang 22.1.0), target wasm32-wasip1
  Runtime:   node:wasi preview1 (standalone WASI — no Emscripten JS glue)
  Configure: --host=wasm32-wasi --disable-openmp --disable-pthreads
             --disable-simd --disable-mpfr --disable-lto --disable-naview
             --disable-unittests --disable-tty-colors --without-svm
             --without-gsl --without-swig --without-perl --without-python
             --without-forester --without-kinfold --without-rnalocmin
             --without-rnaxplorer --without-doc --without-cla --without-check
  Notes:     bundled dlib-based equilibrium-concentration solver excluded (not
             used by RNAfold; pulls sockets/threads absent in WASI). Built-in
             Turner-2004 energy parameters — no external parameter file needed.
